  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gender Budgeting in Ukraine</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Genderbudgetering i Ukraine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The intervention&apos;s intended outcome is to increase the economic efficiency and transparency of budget allocations that take into account the different needs of both gender.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Projektets l&#xe5;ngsiktiga m&#xe5;l &#xe4;r att bidra till att &#xf6;ka den ekonomiska effektiviteten inom budgetallokeringar som beaktar m&#xe4;ns och kvinnors olika behov. GRB (Gender Responsive Budgeting)-projektet i Ukraina initierades av landets Finansdepartement som visar engagemang och f&#xf6;rst&#xe5;else f&#xf6;r vikten av GRB inom p&#xe5;g&#xe5;ende reformer av budgetprocessen. Projektet kommer att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra budgetprocessen genom st&#xe4;rkt integrering av j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet.

Det h&#xe4;r &#xe4;r en f&#xf6;rl&#xe4;ngning av det p&#xe5;g&#xe5;ende projektet till 2020-12-30 och SEK 23 895 266 l&#xe4;ggs till. De ut&#xf6;kade aktiviteterna inkluderar institutionalisering av GRB, arbete med utbildningsinstitutioner och ett inkluderande av GRB i l&#xe4;roplaner f&#xf6;r tj&#xe4;nstem&#xe4;n f&#xf6;r att p&#xe5; s&#xe5; s&#xe4;tt st&#xe4;rka deras kompetens och s&#xe4;kerst&#xe4;lla h&#xe5;llbar implementering av GRB vid Finansdepartementet.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ultimate goal of the project is to contribute to increased economic efficiency and effectiveness in budget allocations that take into account different needs of both women and men. The GRB project in Ukraine was initiated by the Ministry of Finance of Ukraine (MoF) which demonstrates a commitment and understanding of the importance of GRB in enhancing the ongoing public finance reform. The project will improve the budget process by introducing gender equality through a socio-economic analysis method.

The Project started in 2013. This is an extension of the Project till 31-12-2020. The new extended activities cover GRB institualisation, work with educational establishments and to include the GRB into the curricula of civil servants and training to ensure a sustainable provision of skilled practitioners in GRB.</narrative>
  </description>
